WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.530
- The whole shape surprised me.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.270
- There are many curves in that building

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:12.900
and there are also two emblematic cuts.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.230
- I will tell you what the
construction authorities

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.780
said about the house.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.190
They said, it's the "Tear"
or "The Eye of the God."

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.670
I mainly see a teardrop.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:28.273
The Eye of the God is the sun
who comes all over the place.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.601
Hello! My name is George
and welcome to our home.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:39.018
(Bright, cheerful music)

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.040
I live in Heraklion.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.543
We decided to buy this
ground because of the view.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.330
So, we are entering the main living room.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:01.273
This room is the room of light.
You have a lot of sunlight.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.490
In Crete, we are people
who live with the light.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:10.290
Light is all over. It's very aggressive.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:15.290
The curve in front of the house
is uh, philosophically the

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.273
resistance of the concrete to the sun.

00:01:18.273 --> 00:01:20.390
- (Tilemachos) It seems
the house necessarily

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.600
would face this radiant sun.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.960
It should be more
receptive, it should be bent

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.673
by the sun's course from East to West.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.610
- You will go to the kitchen
where, if you have a good cook,

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.650
you can prepare something fantastic to eat

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:45.113
because Crete has a lovely
variety of very good food.

00:01:46.395 --> 00:01:48.250
- (Tilemachos) The
living room is in between

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.820
the cantilevered volume
and the volume of the base,

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:56.343
which acts as a podium and
hosts the sleeping quarters.

00:01:57.816 --> 00:02:01.580
- (George) Most of what
is going on in the house,

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.560
you cannot imagine that from the outside.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.970
Going up the staircase,
one enters the guest room

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.580
that is in contact with
two open air spaces.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:16.433
The one is evident on the
facade, it is its main cut.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:21.180
The other one is completely
hidden from public view.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.760
It is a cut of the roof underneath which

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.603
one may find an open air bath.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.760
- I wouldn't advise you to jump in it,

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.970
but it's very nice

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:34.290
to cool your body in the very hot nights

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.133
or days of the summer.
And we have a lot of them.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.120
The other part is also very interesting,

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.513
because at that part,
you have the Tear of God.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.923
And that's the view.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.810
That's the head of Zeus

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.853
who's very kindly to us in Crete.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:03.340
So now for the easy part,
I will take the elevator

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.123
to show you the rest of the house.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.583
Hello again.

00:03:09.905 --> 00:03:13.430
So here we are entering our main bedroom.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:16.020
This is the master bedroom where we sleep.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.883
We have two more for the kids.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.060
So I'll show you my
secret place in the house.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:28.320
And my secret place is very
easy to access because you can

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.273
open the trap and you just
have to go downstairs.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:39.480
It's meant to be a place where
it's quiet and I can rest.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.941
Fortunately enough,
sometimes I can do that.

00:03:42.941 --> 00:03:46.010
(Upbeat music)

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:50.420
Let me show you, last but
not least, one other thing

00:03:51.796 --> 00:03:56.796
that is one of my demands
that I had for this house.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.780
So this is my playground for adults.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:05.730
It's meant to put a car on
it and to turn it around

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.473
so you don't need to maneuver here.

00:04:14.547 --> 00:04:17.733
(Cheerful music)

00:04:17.733 --> 00:04:20.600
- (Tilemachos) This is one
of the most peculiar designs

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.523
that we have tried.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.350
And I had certain doubts about,

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.370
not the architecture itself,

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:34.300
I was more concerned about
its relation to the city.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.933
But then I said, okay, we have to try.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.243
I think that they
essentially work together.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:47.110
They get more alive in my
eyes because of each other.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:52.160
That neighborhood was invigorated
by this playful house.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.440
And this playful house is in a

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.693
sculptural dialogue with its neighbors.

00:04:57.962 --> 00:05:01.462
(Background music fades)

